  "id": "DrugBank_DB00136 - MONDO_6946",
  "verbalization": "Calcitriol is implicated in the pathogenesis of Renal Osteodystrophy through a series of interconnected pathways involving calcium and phosphate homeostasis. The evidence suggests that Calcitriol, through its indication of Hypophosphatemia (disease) and Hypercalcemia Disease, leads to the production of Calcifediol, which in turn is associated with Renal Osteodystrophy. This chain of indications implies that Calcitriol may influence phosphate metabolism, potentially leading to the development of Renal Osteodystrophy. The presence of multiple pathways involving Calcitriol and Renal Osteodystrophy highlights the role of Calcitriol in modulating calcium and phosphate levels, which are critical for maintaining bone and renal health. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of Calcitriol in the regulation of calcium homeostasis, which could contribute to the development of Renal Osteodystrophy.",
